		{"id":"a1f4a83b50eebfb3","type":"group","x":605,"y":-1000,"width":810,"height":740,"color":"1","label":"Apple Music"},
		{"id":"753cf89b0e4f1521","type":"group","x":-320,"y":-1080,"width":840,"height":545,"color":"#1068c6","label":"Steam Controller"},
		{"id":"0166f4a98aae8aae","type":"text","text":"## The Good","x":-9,"y":-118,"width":249,"height":85,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"211dfb4af79a3718","type":"text","text":"#### Steam Controller","x":148,"y":-640,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"#1068c6"},
		{"id":"5747e8fdb90861ec","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314165248.png","x":186,"y":-850,"width":175,"height":139},
		{"id":"03de1559d78ecc23","type":"text","text":"- Play & Immersion\n- Game Controller\n\n\n","x":171,"y":-993,"width":205,"height":61,"color":"#1068c6"},
		{"id":"1c298a92a8246e7b","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nThe Steam Controller is very effective and efficient to use once you learn how to use it. It’s incredible, especially for any mouse interfaces!\n**Satisfaction**\nIt is satisfying to use, but due to its age, the vibration motor and tactile feelings isn’t up to modern standards.\n**Learnability / Memorabilty**\nDifficult. It’s very different to a normal controller, since instead of a stick and dpad, it uses two touch pads. \n**Safety**\nThere is nothing to report here.\n\n\n","x":-275,"y":-1020,"width":368,"height":411,"color":"#1068c6"},
		{"id":"8656c26f22635e4b","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314163503.png","x":684,"y":-940,"width":91,"height":197},
		{"id":"d41a72457807790c","type":"text","text":"#### Apple Music","x":727,"y":-660,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"18517ab3b87701dd","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314163522.png","x":925,"y":-488,"width":91,"height":197},
		{"id":"85eae09ab6dd1adf","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314163527.png","x":926,"y":-940,"width":91,"height":197},
		{"id":"a61ec0b3a0ae6d24","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314163514.png","x":805,"y":-489,"width":91,"height":198},
		{"id":"5bf2812bc1d7300b","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314163510.png","x":806,"y":-940,"width":91,"height":197},
		{"id":"92b008c15874fed3","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nGood. Most important functions are at most one or two clicks away and there is minimal delay.\n**Satisfaction**\nEasy to use, beautiful design\n**Learnability / Memorabilty**\nEverything is pretty clearly labeled and has iconography. Some Features like Automix might need some introduction first, but are easily memorized after.\n**Safety**\n“Dangerous” functions like removing albums require confirmation.\nthere’s also the system wide “shake to undo” on iOS, which works with apple Music\n\n","x":1065,"y":-940,"width":310,"height":480,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"d14033701f0e16bf","type":"text","text":"- Consumption & Lifestyle\n- Mobile","x":1095,"y":-360,"width":250,"height":69,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"9f0b1f2f0dd52219","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314163517.png","x":683,"y":-489,"width":92,"height":198},
		{"id":"3e1b1c3576b4ebe6","x":-1760,"y":-876,"width":400,"height":225,"type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/20210201205420_1.jpg"},
		{"id":"66f83dd3c23341f6","x":-1760,"y":-584,"width":400,"height":225,"type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/20211001230800_1.jpg"},
		{"id":"b2e043ddb2776847","x":-1760,"y":-304,"width":400,"height":225,"type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/20250301203718_1.jpg"},
		{"id":"743b3bd99aacb844","x":-1760,"y":-1162,"width":400,"height":225,"type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/359320_20260120221056_1.png"},
		{"id":"44cbb1e68c156dc4","type":"text","text":"#### Elite: Dangerous","x":-1160,"y":-191,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"8d89c278d5c98655","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nMost Elite: Dangerous players play the game using a HOTAS *(Hands on Throttle and Stick)*. So the ship UI is designed to work well when using one. The entire UI is easily navigable using just the hat of a HOTAS. It’s easy and fast to achieve whatever you’re trying to do. \n**Satisfaction**\nThe UI sounds are incredibly satisfying.\n**Learnability / Memorabilty**\nUnfortunately, it takes a long time to learn, due to the large amount of features and options you have in your ship. That holds true for the entire game. \n**Safety**\nThere is minimal safety, you can easily make a mistake, like for example ejecting a valuable piece of cargo. But this usually isn’t a big issue. \n\n\n\n","x":-1170,"y":-784,"width":520,"height":425,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"230a3b38bb66a5ad","type":"text","text":"- Play & Immersion\n- Desktop Game (Space Sim)\n\n\n","x":-760,"y":-231,"width":280,"height":79,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"9082a3903e9f8695","x":-1360,"y":267,"width":300,"height":400,"type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314171811.png"},
		{"id":"1c83a780433877f3","x":-1360,"y":707,"width":300,"height":400,"type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314171826.png"},
		{"id":"61b0416c9350d04c","x":-1032,"y":707,"width":300,"height":400,"type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314171832.png"},
		{"id":"c6c1cbbd407aac3e","type":"text","text":"- Consumption & Lifestyle\n- Blender\n\n\n","x":-940,"y":308,"width":415,"height":86,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"f780b41731aaa346","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nThis blender just requires you to put the cup in and push and twist. Gets teh job done\n**Satisfaction**\nIt’s very satisfying to use! \n**Learnability / Memorabilty**\nIncredibly easy to learn since it just push and twist! The twist is optional even! \n**Safety**\nI haven’t figured out a way how to hurt yourself during regular operation of the device.\n\n\n","x":-598,"y":707,"width":438,"height":310,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"1a3e2f19ba208f76","type":"text","text":"#### Zoe’s Blender","x":-410,"y":321,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"f49f50b06147677d","x":766,"y":41,"width":188,"height":199,"type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314170612.png"},
		{"id":"279d1f010c98e374","x":1015,"y":38,"width":400,"height":202,"type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314170649.png"},
		{"id":"fa844296f4c68b5b","x":396,"y":54,"width":320,"height":172,"type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/attachments/Pasted image 20260314170600.png"},
		{"id":"3b1d635dc059445b","type":"text","text":"#### Github Desktop","x":396,"y":302,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"1017ff1cabcf99f6","x":400,"y":512,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6","type":"text","text":"- Creation & Operation\n- Desktop"},
		{"id":"d18869a38eb45368","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nMost important git functions are easily accessible in the ui\n**Satisfaction**\nIt isn’t really “satisfying” in the general sense, because it’s only there to assist with commits, and ideally, the developer shouldn’t get distracted.\n**Learnability / Memorabilty**\nIf you’re familiar with git, the Github Desktop interface is simple to learn and use.\n**Safety**\nThere are confirmation pop ups, but you can easily lose a lot of work if you’re being a little clumsy! That usually doesn’t happen though in day to day use.\n\n\n","x":920,"y":432,"width":438,"height":390,"color":"6"}
	],
